-- title:
--   Finite type of the two chart rings of the integral model
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian unique factorisation domain (a commutative domain that is Noetherian and a unique factorisation monoid), let $K_0$ be a field that is a fraction field of $R$, and let $F$ be a field carrying compatible $R$- and $K_0$-algebra structures, the $R$-algebra structure being induced by that of $K_0$ (a scalar tower $R \to K_0 \to F$). Let $j \in F$ be nonzero and transcendental over $R$, i.e. not a root of any nonzero polynomial with coefficients in $R$. Assume that $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K_0(j)$ obtained by adjoining $j$ to $K_0$ inside $F$, and that $F$ is separable over $K_0(j)$. Then both chart subalgebras of $F$ are $R$-algebras of finite type: the subalgebra $\mathtt{chartAlgFin}$ consisting of all $x \in F$ that are integral over the $R$-subalgebra $R[j]$ of $F$ generated by $j$, and the subalgebra $\mathtt{chartAlgInf}$ consisting of all $x \in F$ integral over the $R$-subalgebra $R[j^{-1}]$ generated by $j^{-1}$. No smoothness, properness or geometric hypothesis on $F$ beyond finiteness and separability over $K_0(j)$ is required.
--
--   The two subalgebras are the coordinate rings of the two affine charts whose Spectra are glued along the middle chart to form the two-chart integral model [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) of a curve with a transcendental coordinate $j$; finite type of both rings is the basic hypothesis under which that model is a scheme of finite type over $R$. It is a base-generic version of the corresponding statement for the Igusa-type integral model over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ with $K_0 = \mathbb{Q}$ and $j$ the modular function, and it is invoked throughout the later development of the model, for instance in the construction of divisors and of étale coordinates on the charts.
